<article article-type="research-article" xml:lang="en" dtd-version="1.3">
  <front>
    <article-meta>
      <title-group>
        <article-title>Complex tables with rich cells</article-title>
      </title-group>
      <contrib-group>
        <contrib contrib-type="author"><string-name>Test Author</string-name></contrib>
      </contrib-group>
    </article-meta>
  </front>
  <body>
    <sec id="sec:tables">
      <title>Two related tables</title>
      <p>The body also carries a formula <inline-formula><tex-math><![CDATA[x^2]]></tex-math></inline-formula>,
        a citation <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="bib-smith2020">Smith</xref>, and a cross-reference to
        <xref ref-type="table" rid="first">the first table</xref>.</p>
      <table-wrap id="first">
        <label>1</label>
        <caption><p>A multi-row header with spans, plus a formula, a citation, and a table footnote in cells.</p></caption>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th rowspan="2">Sample</th>
              <th colspan="2">Measurements</th>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th>energy</th>
              <th>note</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>A</td>
              <td><inline-formula><tex-math><![CDATA[E=mc^2]]></tex-math></inline-formula></td>
              <td>baseline<xref ref-type="fn" rid="tf-1">*</xref></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>B</td>
              <td align="right"><inline-formula><tex-math><![CDATA[\rho^2]]></tex-math></inline-formula></td>
              <td>see <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="bib-smith2020">Smith</xref></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <table-wrap-foot>
          <fn id="tf-1"><label>*</label><p>A footnote attached to the first table.</p></fn>
        </table-wrap-foot>
      </table-wrap>
      <table-wrap id="second">
        <label>2</label>
        <caption><p>A second table whose cell cross-references the first.</p></caption>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Quantity</th><th colspan="3">Values by group</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>derived from Table <xref ref-type="table" rid="first">1</xref></td>
              <td colspan="3">pooled estimate</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </table-wrap>
    </sec>
  </body>
  <back>
    <ref-list>
      <ref id="bib-smith2020">
